#N canvas 40 40 1000 760 12;
#X text 20 40 cz4~ against Arturia CZ V: comparison recordings;
#X text 20 64 1. Import the test tones into CZ V: test/tones/cz101/test01.syx ... test12.syx (CZ-101 data \, the usual form). If CZ V does not take them \, try tones/dump \, tones/cz1 or tones/cz1dump \, or the banks test/cz4test-bank-*.syx. With CZ-101 data set the velocity by hand for test 5 (DCA 15 \, DCW 8 on line 1). Leave the CZ V settings at their defaults (volume \, effects off \, no unison \, poly)., f 120;
#X text 20 118 2. Route: Pd MIDI out -> CZ V MIDI in (IAC driver on the Mac) \, CZ V audio out -> Pd audio in 1+2 (a loopback such as BlackHole 2ch \, or the interface). The meter below shows the input level. Set channel to CZ V's MIDI channel., f 120;
#X text 20 172 3. Choose a test \, select its tone in CZ V \, press run. The sequence goes to CZ V and to cz4~ at once \, both are recorded into test/rec/ (czv-testNN.wav \, cz4-testNN.wav). With all on \, the tests run one after the other: for that CZ V must change tones on program change (pc on \, program = test number - 1) \, otherwise run them one by one., f 120;
#X text 20 226 4. Test 7 needs portamento on (time 50) and bend range 2 in CZ V. All others: portamento off. Then: python3 test/cz_compare.py test/rec (in the repository: tools/cz_compare.py cz4/test/rec) writes test/rec/report.md with plots. Needs numpy., f 120;
#X text 20 300 test;
#X floatatom 60 300 3 1 12 0 - czt-selv czt-sel;
#X text 110 300 run;
